id: pm-dwj33e
title: "ADR: Graph structural ratchets measure recorded nodes and informative edges"
description: Authorize the graph assurance node and edge floors to move from diagnostic totals to invariant-bearing recorded-node and informative-edge populations.
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: adr,assurance,governance,graph,ratchet,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-13T09:51:55.349Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T10:09:35.258Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T09:52:12.680Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T09:52:12.680Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The node floor reads profile.recorded_nodes and excludes missing or external placeholders.; The edge floor reads profile.informative_edges after a union deduction for redundant and contradictory rows.; Redundancy and ordering contradictions have independent ceilings so cleanup tightens rather than weakens governance.
goal: truthful-graph-assurance
objective: Prevent placeholder and repairable-edge debt from being required by structural floors.
value: Graph cleanup can reduce defects without requiring a privileged floor relaxation.
impact: CI separately preserves real item and informative relationship populations while allowing redundancy and contradictions to shrink.
outcome: "Recorded-node and informative-edge floors ratchet independently from missing placeholders, redundant shortcuts, and contradictory storage rows."
why_now: The final legacy cleanup is mechanically correct but the old total-edge floor treats the repair as structural loss.
parent: pm-m2u1
resolution: "Accepted ADR: graph assurance now separates diagnostic totals from recorded-node and informative-edge invariant populations."
expected_result: "Graph cleanup can remove missing placeholders and non-informative edges without weakening the structural floors, while independent ceilings prevent debt growth."
actual_result: "SDK audit fields, durable-baseline compatibility, exact contradiction evidence, and blocking assurance declarations were implemented and verified on the live corpus."
