  "2026-08-13T09:52:11.134Z","harness:codex","Evidence before acceptance: live graph audit after the changelog-safe cleanup reports nodes=2463 and recorded_nodes=2463; edges=12117, redundant_edges=67, ordering_contradiction_edges=0, and informative_edges=12050. All graph finding families are zero. The new fields are SDK-owned, deterministic, persisted in durable baselines with legacy defaults, and covered by focused tests."
  "2026-08-13T09:55:25.007Z","harness:codex","Acceptance follow-up: the first full tracker-context-quality dry-run blocked exactly because this newly closed Decision lacked resolution fields (296 vs ceiling 295). The item now carries resolution, expected_result, and actual_result; this demonstrates the existing validation ratchet caught a real closeout omission."
  "2026-08-13T10:05:57.136Z","harness:codex","Assurance evidence: tracker-context-quality correctly blocked the four newly added generic related edges at 6057 against ceiling 6053. They are now directional discovered_from provenance edges to the four source items, preserving graph context without weakening the related-edge ratchet."
  "2026-08-13T10:06:13.935Z","harness:codex","Correction and completion: the first dependency mutation was rejected because the supported add flag is --dep, so the immediately preceding comment described intended state before it existed. The corrected atomic update has now replaced all four related rows with discovered_from rows; live metadata is authoritative."
  "2026-08-13T10:09:35.258Z","harness:codex","SDK compatibility evidence: the surface gate classified the expanded existing interfaces conservatively. New graph fields were made optional for consumer-authored fixtures and legacy snapshots, runtime producers always populate them, durable decoding supplies legacy defaults, and the public snapshot was updated with this Decision plus pm-h06944 as the explicit rationale. Build, package/example typechecks, and surface re-check pass."
close_reason: "Accepted: graph structural floors use recorded nodes and informative edges; diagnostic totals remain visible and redundancy/contradictions receive independent ceilings."
body: "## Context\nThe existing graph node and edge floors consume diagnostic totals. Missing placeholders inflate nodes; witnessed redundancy and contradictory ordering rows inflate edges. A repair therefore lowers a floor even when the information-bearing graph is unchanged.\n\n## Decision\nStructural assurance floors are denominated over `profile.recorded_nodes` and `profile.informative_edges`. Diagnostic `nodes` and `edges` remain public. Informative edges equal deduplicated directed edges minus the union of witnessed redundant edge identities and structured ordering rows proven to contradict scalar blockers. Independent ceilings govern redundancy and contradiction populations.\n\n## Consequences\nRemoving a placeholder cannot fail the recorded-node floor. Removing a redundant or contradictory edge cannot fail the informative-edge floor. Deleting real work or an information-bearing relationship still lowers a blocking floor and requires an explicit Decision. The bounded redundancy algorithm and its counting basis remain visible in the audit profile and documentation."
